{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Get observations"},"description":"Read up to 20 series ids or a member dataset with named dimension filters. One call with dataset and no filter returns every member of the dataset (all 16 voivodeships of a voivodeship dataset), so no call per member is needed. A family that is not a member dataset (pay or flat prices by voivodeship) is read with all its ids in one call, e.g. the 16 ids of one podziemie_search_series answer with limit 16 (its default is 10), not one call per id. Returns the last 24 periods by default, at most 1,500 cells and 24,000 characters, with Polish citations, licences and a cursor plus data links for the rest; the text holds every value too. When the answer holds only part of the request, its text starts \"Series a to b of n\" and names what is missing: call again with nextCursor before comparing the series.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"nextCursor from the previous answer.","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"dataset":{"description":"A member dataset, e.g. \"bezrobocie-wojewodztwa\"; use instead of ids.","maxLength":80,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"detail":{"description":"full adds raw values, coverage, readingBasis (concise states it in each citation) and identity fields.","enum":["concise","full"],"type":"string"},"filter":{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":40,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},{"items":{"maxLength":40,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"maxItems":100,"minItems":1,"type":"array"}]},"description":"With dataset: {<dimension>: code | [codes] | \"*\"}; omitted means every member.","propertyNames":{"maxLength":40,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"from":{"description":"First period, in each series' periodShape.","maxLength":16,"minLength":1,"pattern":"^[0-9A-Za-z-]+$","type":"